Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: release idle IPU4 video devices

The legacy IPU4 ISYS driver holds a power reference for each open video
node. Keeping that node open across stop/start leaves the rear sensor
unable to restart. Release idle video nodes after enumeration and scoped
configuration, buffer export and capture leases. Restore links and the
complete configured format before capture, preserve shared entity ownership
and quarantine failed STREAMOFF state. Cache RAW validation layout while
enumerating so application-thread validation needs no closed-device ioctl.

Limit this lifecycle to media driver intel-ipu6 with model ipu4p. Other
Simple pipelines retain their existing device lifetime and validation.
The unscoped prototype passed two full-resolution 55-frame rear captures
with one configuration and no external wait; scoped package validation is
a separate required step. No public ABI changes.

---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
